## What decided it
The pre-ride read was the whole heat. `null-floors.json` published this seed's floor and the ten-second probe reproduced it **to the hash** — proving era 6 moved this map's rendering, not its rules (zero of the eight pins name it). That freed the budget for the two era systems, which handed me the contract: the secure is `wave ≥ 12` **AND** one completed light hold, a hold is a living powered `sentry_beacon` inside a radius-4 disc at (−28,−6) held unbroken through telegraph+squall (33 s), and telegraph opens at t = 60/161/262 against a wave-12 gate at t = 360.

**The near-miss worth naming:** eleven of my twelve candidates inside that disc — including the light stake's own centre — answered `UNREACHABLE: BUILD target is outside buildable terrain`, all at z ≤ −4, despite the zone being declared z −30…18. Only **(−28,−3)** landed; the legal band is about two units deep. A rider offering just the published site coordinate would report this contract unwinnable. The beacon stood at t = 19.17 and the hold latched at t = 60.03, the telegraph tick itself.

## The margin I left
Gold, the only free ranking axis: **200 of a 200 default cap**, with `goldPanned` frozen at 645 from t ≈ 312. Both `stockpile` rungs (safe here — no thief on the roster) were emitted once, at t = 265.7, **both at the same coordinate**, and my own late-spend floor then wiped the order 4.3 s later, mid-walk. Two one-line cures are named in the report; a stockpile landing at t ≈ 250 is worth ~250–300 banked on an identical secure.

